lisa-selfreview:
pass 2 (strict) verdict: request_changes
- [medium] validation-bases-mismatch (AgentConfigEditorDrawer → useOverlayDraft clientIssues): client validation runs against EVERY loaded base (stale, report-mode), while the API validates only ValidationBases (fresh apply-mode instances, else the latest-reported apply-mode one, else standalone). A problem introduced only for a report-mode host blocks Review although the API would save. Fix: compute the same set client-side (validationInstanceIds) and use it for validation and the advisory policy-only fallback; keep all bases for removals.
- [medium] file-plugin-without-source-blocks (validation.ts effectiveIssues): the "needs a source" check only looks at plugins the overlay touches, so a file plugin that already lacks a source becomes a BLOCKING issue as soon as the overlay touches it (the R59 baseline with overlay {} never sees it). Fix: check every effective plugin; the baseline then marks file-origin ones non-blocking.
